# Locked flows — FF Diamond

The user will change functionality later. Until they explicitly name a flow to change:

- Do not change ads flow at all: AdsGate, AdsBinder, AdsSdk, AdsRepository, InstallSource, web/interstitial/app-open counts, banner/native bind, goNext/onBack ad gates, afterDefault interstitial.
- Do not change other flows: FunnelStep names, FunnelNav destinations except Intro after Set Default, organic vs paid, Splash routing, Set Default → afterDefault ads → Intro → Language, Language → DiamondHome (organic) or the paid funnel. Paid order after Language: Gender → Age → Favorite Character → Favorite Pet → Game Mode → Favorite Weapon → Favorite Vehicle → Favorite Bundle → Favorite Emote → Get Started.
- Do not add/remove/reorder funnel steps. Extra onboarding UIs must map onto existing steps.
- Keep ads/flow view IDs: `funnel_root`, `ad_native`, `ad_banner`, `default_continue`, `default_continue_hand`.
- UI, colors, layouts, and copy may change. Flow and ads must stay identical.

Do not reply with file lists or git-style change reports. Give the user-facing result only.
